{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"67aa plan-review round 4: BLOCK (2 blockers). B1 [E6/E2]: referenced an 'admission report' sink for selector tier but never specified path/format/fields, no AC proving it written. FIX: dropped the phantom file entirely; runner returns an in-memory summary (admitted/withheld ids, drift entries, spend) asserted by tests; spec carries no posture/tier field (not eval-spec schema). B2 [G6]: per-criterion atomicity false - spec-file write and ledger finalize() are two unordered disk ops; crash between them corrupts resume either way (ledger-first-crash loses spec while charged; spec-first-crash leaves a spec the no-shadowing SKIP mistakes for a built-in). FIX: STRICT ORDER atomic spec os.replace FIRST then finalize() SECOND; ledger run_id is sole resume oracle; no-shadowing scoped to PACKAGED built-ins only (a same-id .rebar/evals file is a prior artifact, idempotently overwritten, never skipped). Invariant: finalized criterion always has its spec. Added crash-orphan resume AC + packaged-only skip AC. Desc 7944 chars, 11 ACs. Round 5 running."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788422030250258001,"uuid":"87a62f15-e34c-4b0d-942a-2f1b811b3880"}